<g>COLOR KEYWORDS - SECONDARY STATS<1>
Colors provide bonuses to secondary stats:
  <r>RED<1> - Hit Points (+level bonus)
  <g>GREEN<1> - Movement Points (+level bonus)
  <b>BLUE<1> - Mana Points (+level bonus)
  <p>PURPLE<1> - Hit Points/Mana (half value of each)
  <Y>YELLOW<1> - Vision (+level bonus)
  <k>GREY/GRAY<1> - Can Be Seen (+level bonus)
  <w>WHITE<1> - Light (+1 only)
  <k>BLACK<1> - Can Be Seen (+1), Light (-1), displays as gray

<g>COLOR CODES<1>
Both color words and MUD color codes work:
  <r>Red<1>, <g>Green<1>, <b>Blue<1>, <p>Purple<1>, <Y>Yellow<1>, <k>Grey<1>, etc.
  Bold versions also work: <R>RED<1>, <G>GREEN<1>, <B>BLUE<1>, etc.

<g>EXAMPLES<1>
"A <r>red<1> lion" on unequipped head at level 20:
  +2 STR, +2 Hit Points

"A <g>green<1> dragon" on unequipped body at level 30:
  +2 STR, +1 SPE, +3 Movement Points

"A <p>purple<1> tiger" on unequipped arm at level 20:
  +2 STR, +2 DEX, +1 Hit Points, +1 Mana Points

"A <k>gray<1> eagle" on unequipped neck at level 30:
  +3 PER, +3 Can Be Seen

"A <w>white<1> mongoose" on unequipped hand at any level:
  +3 SPE, +1 Light

"A <k>black<1> bear" on unequipped foot at any level:
  +3 CON, +1 Can Be Seen, -1 Light

<g>TIPS<1>
- Remove equipment to activate tattoo bonuses
- Higher level = stronger bonuses
- Plan tattoo placement for maximum benefit
- Color words take priority over color codes
- Only first animal and color in each tattoo count

